  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins1900.html",
  "prefLabel": "Ins 1902.11 Permitted Compensation Arrangements",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 1902.11 Permitted Compensation Arrangements.\n\n(a) For purposes of this section, “compensation” means pecuniary or nonpecuniary remuneration of any kind relating to the sale or renewal of the policy or certificate, including but not limited to bonuses, gifts, prizes, awards, and finders' fees.\n\n(b) An insurer or other entity may provide commission or other compensation to an agent or other representative for the sale of a Medicare supplement policy or certificate only if the first year commission or other first year compensation is no more than 200 percent of the commission or other compensation paid for selling or servicing the policy or certificate in the second year or period.\n\n(c) The commission or other compensation provided in subsequent renewal years shall be the same as that provided in the second year or period.\n\n(d) No entity shall provide compensation to its agents or other producers, and no agent or producer shall receive compensation greater than the renewal compensation payable by the replacing insurer on renewal policies or certificates if an existing policy or certificate is replaced.\n\nSource. #1900, eff 1-1-82; ss by #4287, eff 7-1-87; ss by #5119, eff 4-25-91; ss by #5656, eff 7-1-93; ss by #7017, INTERIM, eff 7-1-99, EXPIRED: 10-29-99\n\nNew. #8555, eff 2-1-06, EXPIRED: 2-1-14\n\nNew. #11014, eff 1-8-16; ss by #14661, eff 7-23-26, EXPIRES: 7-23-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins1900.html"
